## Lore

The Great Lakes, the Missouri and Mississippi rivers and the Gulf of Mexico all
lie close to the Coalition States, which led to the Naval Advisory Commission,
a branch of the Army first set up to deal with the ley-line-haunted Great
Lakes. The Emperor intends it to become a separate CS Navy within a few years,
and is quietly building a naval headquarters at Lone Star.

Officially the Nautical Specialists are Sea Devils; everyone calls them
Naughty Boys, to their annoyance. They are trained for boats, warships, SCUBA,
underwater demolitions and coastal work, and are less formidable on land.
Until the Navy exists they keep Army ranks.

## GM Notes

The service is treated as a stepchild by the General Staff and often gets
equipment last, and many senior officers regard the posting as punishment.
The younger noncoms and junior officers who came up in it see its future.

Small, close-knit crews of Nautical Specialists and RPA troops on patrol boats
get more freedom than most CS soldiers, and have a reputation as independent
lone wolves.
